\f0\fs24 \cf2 Step into the Green Room, a space that reveals the private side of Giuseppe Bagatti Valsecchi, who, like many aristocrats of his time, had a personal chamber all to himself. Here, every element tells a story of style and seclusion: the room is remarkably preserved, just as it was when Giuseppe lived in it. Every detail remains in place, just as it once was, the furnishings, the atmosphere. Only a few small elements are missing, such as the cabinet beside the bed, the wallpaper, and the rugs that in other rooms added warmth and comfort. Yet even without these, the room retains its charm. It was designed for rest and privacy, and it still evokes the feeling of a personal retreat, a peaceful corner within the heart of this house.\
